### 5. G-T12 Mac-native checks

| Check | How |
|---|---|
| arm64 | `uname -m` gives `arm64`. Run `file` on the runtime Python, ffmpeg and any shipped binary: each must be arm64. |
| No Rosetta | `sysctl -n sysctl.proc_translated` gives 0 in the shells you used. `/usr/bin/pgrep oahd` shows whether Rosetta is even installed: note it, never install it. |
| No admin | the installer never ran `sudo` and never asked for a password (check the install log and the transcript) |
| Quarantine | `xattr -l` on the downloaded and installed files shows no `com.apple.quarantine`, and nothing asked to disable Gatekeeper |
| Per-user folders | `~/Library/Fonts`, `~/Library/Application Support/Adobe/CEP/extensions`, UPIA's per-user install for the `.ccx`, `~/Library/LaunchAgents` (if used): exactly what the installer README says |
| TCC prompts | which privacy prompts appeared (Files & Folders, Automation, ...), when, and whether the product explained them first. Ask Yunus to read each one out. |
| macOS version | `sw_vers`, and the oldest version you could test. The supported range is macOS 13 to current. |

